From: enfs-dkms
Subject: [PATCH] fs/nfs/internal.h: extern struct file_system_type enfs_fs_type (#20)

Adds the forward declaration for the new "enfs" filesystem type.
The actual definition lives in fs_context.c (next patch).

Sibling of nfs_fs_type's extern; same conditional pattern as the
nfs4_fs_type guard (CONFIG-gated).

Issue: #20

---
 fs/nfs/internal.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/fs/nfs/internal.h
+++ b/fs/nfs/internal.h
@@ -278,6 +278,9 @@

 /* fs_context.c */
 extern struct file_system_type nfs_fs_type;
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ENFS)
+extern struct file_system_type enfs_fs_type;
+#endif

 /* pagelist.c */
 extern int __init nfs_init_nfspagecache(void);
